<title>INDIA: India's SBI 1996/97 net seen higher.</title>
<headline>India's SBI 1996/97 net seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Bank of India's (SBI) net profit is expected to rise 65.97 percent to 13.80 billion rupees in the year ended March 31, 1997, according to a Reuter poll of 28 leading securities and brokerage firms.</p>
<p>Analysts' forecasts ranged from 12.50 billion rupees to 17.50 billion against 8.32 billion in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>SBI is India's largest commercial bank.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SBI  ----PAT seen up 65.97%, sales up 7.57%</p>
<p>			Net profit  1995/96   Net income    1995/96</p>
<p>				 (in million rupees)</p>
<p>Average	     13,801.87  8,316.00   169,060.28  157,155.90</p>
<p>High		  17,500.00		 185,000.00</p>
<p>Low		   12,500.00		 140,000.00</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
